  "note": "POSIX specifies comparator access but no explicit same-thread guarantee. The pinned Apple implementation is source evidence, not an identity assertion about the installed libSystem binary. glibc source is upstream 2.36, while runtime packages retain the separately pinned Debian patch version. Direct invocation and absence of retention/thread dispatch in these implementations support the unsafe binding promise; runtime markers independently check the exercised paths. Zig supplies signature prior art and Rust supplies explicit unwind termination prior art, neither is Silk ABI authority.",
